$MDESC::Type = "VIP";
$MDESC::Text = "<s3><f1>Mission Type: <f0> VIP Assassination" @
         "\n<f1>Planet: <f0> Strategema 00X-5C1" @
         "\n<f1>Weather: <f0> Clear" @
         "\n<f1>Time of Day: <f0> Night" @ 
         "\n<f1># of Teams: <f0> 2" @
	 "\n<f1>Max Bases: <f0> 2/5" @
         "\n\n<f1>Briefing:<f0> The two formost military strategists of the imperial forces have long been engaged in a friendly rivalry.  On many occassions the two have found a reason to take to the practice fields against one another in order to engage in elaborate war games-- as much to attempt to one-up their rival as to test the effectiveness of a military strategy.  Recently a debate has flared up between the two regarding several major historical battles between various tribes and across various unrelated worlds.  All of these major battles were great and showed signs of amazing tacticianship-- but which was the greatest and showed the most shrewed use of all tactical advantages and amenities.  After several days of arguing back and forth, attempting to disuade one another, these two military geniuses decided to take it to the practice field and engage in a mock battle, mimicing the conditions of several of these great historical wars, to determine which victory truly was the most impressive.  \n\nNow both sides are squared off on this remote world of classified location in an attempt to overcome the enemy defenses and win the battle.  Strangely, the ammunition which has been loaded into the weapons appears to be startlingly real.  And despite that fact, neither of the strategists are intent on stopping the exercise.  Apparently the grudge born by both strategists ran deeper and was less friendly than most believed, and what was once a routine training exercise has become a life and death struggle from which only one can emerge alive!\n\nSeek out and kill the enemy Military Strategist while defending your own.  The first team to assassinate the enemy Military Strategist will be declared the victor!";
